  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Calculate the period of the function $f(x)=-3\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(\\frac{8x-\\pi }{4}).$",
  "worked_solution": "Given a function of the form $y=A\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is $\\frac{\\pi }{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that\n\n$$\nf(x)=-3\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(\\frac{8x-\\pi }{4})=-3\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B=2,$ and so the period is $\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$",
